  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the end of three years from the date of this permission.\r\n\r\nReason: In order to comply with the provisions of Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).\r\n\r\n",
    "Condition : 2 - (TIA-IFC-PL-A-)001; 002A; 003; 004; 005B; 006A; 007A; 008; 009; 25-1070 Rev P3; IFC-DOC 03 Site Photos; Arboricultural Impact Assessment report for 7 Inverfoth Close� by Landmark Trees (ref. TIA/7IVF/AIA/01a and dated 10/02/2026); Design & Access Statement by Twist in Architecture Rev B (dated February 2026) and Heritage Statement by HEA ref:H02395 (dated 04.12.2025)\r\n\r\nReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interest of proper planning.\r\n",
    "Condition : 3 - All new external work shall be carried out in materials that resemble, as closely as possible, in colour and texture those of the existing building, unless otherwise specified in the approved application. \r\n\r\nReason: To safeguard the appearance of the premises and the character of the immediate area in accordance with the requirements of policies D1 and D2 of the London Borough of Camden Local Plan 2017 and policies DH1 and DH2 of the Hampstead Neighbourhood Plan 2018-2033. \r\n",
    "Condition : 4 - Prior to the commencement of works on site, tree protection measures shall be installed, working practices and construction methodology adopted in accordance with the document entitled \"Arboricultural Impact Assessment report for 7 Inverfoth Close\" dated 10/02/2026 by Landmark Trees ref. TIA/7IVF/AIA/01a.  All trees on the site, or parts of trees grow from adjoining sites, unless shown on the permitted drawings as being removed, shall be retained and protected from damage in accordance with BS5837:2012 and with the approved protection details. The development shall be monitored by the project arboriculturalist in accordance with the approved report.\n \n\r\n\r\nReason: To ensure that the development will not have an adverse effect on existing trees and in order to maintain the character and amenity of the area in accordance with the requirements of policies A2 and A3 of the Camden Local Plan."
  ],
